{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Cheaper Inference API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Wallet-backed, OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible inference. Authenticate with `Authorization: Bearer ci_live_...` or `x-api-key: ci_live_...`. Both are accepted on every endpoint, and `Authorization` wins if both are present.\n\nEvery successful BUFFERED response carries `request_id` and `billing` at the top level, with the request id and what the request was billed. Messages streams carry them on the terminal `message_delta`, and Responses streams on the terminal `response.completed` or `response.incomplete`. Chat Completions and Completions streams carry neither: reconcile those from the `x-ci-request-id` response header. `billed_cost_usd` is a fixed 6-decimal string, not a number: a JSON float cannot round-trip a micro-dollar amount.\n\nJSON inference bodies may be compressed: `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/completions`, `/v1/responses`, `/v1/messages`, `/v1/messages/count_tokens`, `/v1/images/generations` and `/v1/videos/generations`. Send `Content-Encoding: gzip`, `deflate` or `br` and the body is inflated before parsing, which is how a conversation larger than the 4.5 MB wire limit can be sent. A single encoding only, and a body that inflates past 20 MB is refused with 413 - except on `/v1/messages/count_tokens`, where the inflated ceiling is 4.5 MB. Multipart image edits and the non-inference endpoints read their bodies directly and expect them uncompressed.\n\nThis document covers the customer-facing `/v1` surface only."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://api.cheaperinference.com",
      "description": "Production"
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "BearerAuth": []
    },
    {
      "AnthropicApiKey": []
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Chat",
      "description": "OpenAI-compatible chat and text completion."
    },
    {
      "name": "Images",
      "description": "OpenAI-compatible image generation and canary-gated image editing."
    },
    {
      "name": "Messages",
      "description": "Anthropic Messages. Claude Code integrates here."
    },
    {
      "name": "Responses",
      "description": "OpenAI Responses. Codex integrates here."
    },
    {
      "name": "Decisions",
      "description": "OpenAI Decisions. Typed questions answered with probabilities by decision models such as Jev."
    },
    {
      "name": "Embeddings",
      "description": "OpenAI Embeddings. One vector per input from an embedding model."
    },
    {
      "name": "Models",
      "description": "The catalog, its capabilities and its prices."
    },
    {
      "name": "Usage",
      "description": "What the workspace spent. Requires the usage:read scope."
    },
    {
      "name": "Feedback",
      "description": "Score a completed request."
    },
    {
      "name": "Account",
      "description": "Wallet, savings, experiments, techniques, keys and connected chat channels. Reads need the account:read scope and changes need account:write; neither is on a key by default. This is the surface the MCP server drives."
    },
    {
      "name": "Docs",
      "description": "The product documentation, searchable. Public content, so any valid key can read it without an additional scope. It exists as an endpoint so an assistant can answer 'how do I…' from the shipped text rather than from memory."
    },
    {
      "name": "Keak Code",
      "description": "The opt-in client contract the Keak Code VS Code extension uses: the calling key's technique profile, task budgets and request attribution, alongside the `x-ci-model-lock` and `x-ci-stream-receipt` headers on the inference endpoints. These routes need the `inference` scope, not `account:read`."
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/v1/chat/completions": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "Chat"
        ],
        "summary": "Create a chat completion",
        "operationId": "createChatCompletion",
        "description": "OpenAI-compatible. The request is optimized, served from the exact-match cache when possible, and billed against the wallet. Two opt-in request headers form the client contract Keak Code uses: `x-ci-model-lock` (serve exactly the named model) and `x-ci-stream-receipt` (receipt frames in the stream).",
        "security": [
          {
            "BearerAuth": []
          },
          {
            "AnthropicApiKey": []
          }
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "x-ci-techniques",
            "in": "header",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Set to off to disable optional workspace techniques for a controlled benchmark. Preserves workspace defaults and billing policy; takes precedence over technique opt-in headers.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "off"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "x-ci-prompt-cache",
            "in": "header",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Prompt-cache knob. `passthrough` (default, or the API key's `prompt_cache_mode`) forwards the request unchanged; `on` additionally adds provider cache breakpoints for supported models. For Claude, unmarked requests cache the shared system/tools prefix and growing conversation; caller-supplied cache controls and lifetimes are preserved. `off` removes explicit cache controls, disables sticky affinity for this request and, for models that read a cache marker, prefers routes that forward the body as sent over the marketplace; it does not disable a provider's implicit caching.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "on",
                "off",
                "passthrough"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "x-ci-prompt-cache-scope",
            "in": "header",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Sticky-affinity scope: `session` (default), `user`, or `org`. Scopes the affinity key that keeps a repeated prompt prefix on the same upstream provider so its cache stays warm.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "session",
                "user",
                "org"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "x-ci-prompt-cache-session",
            "in": "header",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Session id read when the scope is `session`. Send one stable value per conversation or agent run. When absent, a string prompt_cache_key in the request body is used. Without either identifier, the tools, opening system instructions and first conversation message identify the session. Affinity remains isolated to the API key.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "x-ci-model-lock",
            "in": "header",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Model Lock. Serve exactly the model named in the body: no model-routing technique, no experiment variant and no admission canary may substitute it. Combined with `X-CI-Experiment` (or a forced experiment variant) it is refused with 400 `model_lock_conflict` before anything is read or reserved. If any stage would still change the model, the request is refused with 500 `model_lock_violation` before reaching a model and nothing is billed. Model routing is held off even when the key, the workspace or `x-ci-route` turns it on. `1` or `true` (any case) turns it on; absent or empty leaves it off. Any other value, including `0` and `false`, is refused with 400 `invalid_contract_header` naming the header in `param`, so a typo never silently means off.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "1",
                "true"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "x-ci-stream-receipt",
            "in": "header",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Receipt mode. On a streamed `/v1/chat/completions` request (`stream: true`), add two standalone SSE frames: an opening frame before the first upstream frame and a final receipt after billing finalize, before `data: [DONE]`. See the `text/event-stream` response. Accepted and ignored on a non-streamed request. `1` or `true` (any case) turns it on; absent or empty leaves it off. Any other value, including `0` and `false`, is refused with 400 `invalid_contract_header` naming the header in `param`, so a typo never silently means off.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "1",
                "true"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "x-ci-vercel-provider",
            "in": "header",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Opt-in strict Vercel upstream provider pin for operator-enabled model/provider pairs. Use the same provider ID on every request to retain provider consistency. Requires Core chat completions; fails rather than falling back to another source. Conflicts with API-key seller routing rules. Does not guarantee a cache hit or change the admitted customer price. Omit for normal routing.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,63}$"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ChatCompletionRequest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful response",
            "headers": {
              "x-ci-zdr": {
                "description": "Whether zero data retention applied to this request. Absent when no policy was recorded.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "true",
                    "false"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "x-ci-discount-percent": {
                "description": "Quoted customer rate discount versus list, not the final effective savings after usage and optimizations. See usage history for the settled effective discount.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "X-Cheaper-Inference-Request-Id": {
                "description": "Request identifier. Legacy name, still emitted; identical to x-ci-request-id.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "uuid"
                }
              },
              "x-ci-request-id": {
                "description": "Request identifier. Canonical going forward.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "uuid"
                }
              },
              "x-ci-tokens-saved": {
                "description": "Input tokens removed by the optimizer.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "x-ci-saved-usd": {
                "description": "Total saved against the provider's list price, in USD.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "x-ci-techniques": {
                "description": "Comma-separated ids of the optimization techniques applied. Empty when none were.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "x-ci-cache": {
                "description": "`hit` or `miss` for the exact-match cache.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "x-ci-prompt-cache-affinity": {
                "description": "Sticky prompt-cache outcome (KEA-5164). One of `hit`, `moved`, `new`, `stale`. `hit` means the request was served on the route its conversation was warm on; `moved` means a warm route was remembered but another route served this turn, so its cache was not reused. Present only when the request carried a cacheable prefix and the affinity mode was not off; the exact-match `cache` header covers the separate response cache.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "x-ci-experiment-variant": {
                "description": "Name of the assigned experiment variant. Present only when the request included X-CI-Experiment and matched a running experiment.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "x-ci-routing-overhead-ms": {
                "description": "Elapsed milliseconds from proxy request start to dispatch of the successful provider attempt, including routing and prior attempts. On an exact-match cache hit, measures elapsed proxy processing time before returning the cached response. Present on successful buffered, streaming, and cached responses.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 0
                }
              },
              "x-ci-model-response-ms": {
                "description": "Elapsed milliseconds from dispatch of the successful provider attempt to its complete response body. Present on successful non-streaming responses; absent on streaming responses and when no provider was called.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 0
                }
              },
              "x-ci-warning": {
                "description": "Present when the request was served with a parameter value other than the one sent, because the model does not accept the value sent. Names the parameter, the value sent and the value used. Example: GPT-6 reasoning_effort \"minimal\" is served as \"low\". A request pinned to a provider is refused with 400 unsupported_parameter instead.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "x-ci-stage-timing": {
                "description": "Optional diagnostic timing breakdown, emitted when PROXY_STAGE_TIMING=1 and a request timer is active. Comma-separated stage=milliseconds entries with total first; zero-duration stages are omitted. Stage names depend on the request path.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "example": "total=1534,auth=258,wallet_hold=128"
                }
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ChatCompletionResponse"
                }
              },
              "text/event-stream": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "Server-sent events. Set `stream: true` on the request to select this. Native Chat streams carry no `cheaper_inference` envelope (KEA-5313): the settled charge is on the usage API (`GET /v1/usage/requests?request_ids=`). In receipt mode (`x-ci-stream-receipt`) two extra `data:` frames are added, each one line of compact JSON whose top-level keys are exactly `type`, `object` and `cheaper_inference` (no `choices`, `id`, `model` or `usage`):\n\n1. Opening (`type: response.cheaper_inference.request`, schema `ReceiptOpeningFrame`), immediately before the first upstream frame. It names the request id, so a stream cut before the end can still be reconciled.\n2. Final (`type: response.cheaper_inference.receipt`, schema `ReceiptFinalFrame`), after billing finalize and before `data: [DONE]`, or before `event: error` when the stream ended incomplete. It carries the charge the ledger settled.\n\nNeither frame is written on a non-streamed, cached or refused response.\n\nOpening example:\n\n```\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.cheaper_inference.request\",\"object\":\"cheaper_inference.request\",\"cheaper_inference\":{\"receipt_version\":1,\"phase\":\"opening\",\"request_id\":\"6f1c2a9e-3b4d-4c5e-8f70-1a2b3c4d5e6f\",\"api_key_id\":\"0b7e9d2c-5a14-4f3b-9c8d-7e6f5a4b3c2d\",\"requested_model\":\"claude-sonnet-4.6\",\"model_lock\":{\"requested\":true,\"enforced\":true}}}\n```\n\nFinal example:\n\n```\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.cheaper_inference.receipt\",\"object\":\"cheaper_inference.receipt\",\"cheaper_inference\":{\"receipt_version\":1,\"phase\":\"final\",\"request_id\":\"6f1c2a9e-3b4d-4c5e-8f70-1a2b3c4d5e6f\",\"api_key_id\":\"0b7e9d2c-5a14-4f3b-9c8d-7e6f5a4b3c2d\",\"requested_model\":\"claude-sonnet-4.6\",\"served_model\":\"claude-sonnet-4.6\",\"model_lock\":{\"requested\":true,\"enforced\":true},\"complete\":true,\"billing\":{\"status\":\"settled\",\"billed_cost_usd\":\"0.004213\",\"currency\":\"USD\",\"usage_known\":true,\"basis\":\"ledger\",\"zero_data_retention\":false},\"tokens\":{\"input\":1820,\"output\":214,\"cache_read\":1536,\"cache_write\":0,\"reasoning\":0},\"prompt_cache_mode\":\"on\",\"techniques\":[{\"slug\":\"model-routing\",\"outcome\":\"skipped\",\"reason\":\"model_lock\",\"tokens_saved\":0,\"version\":null,\"layer\":\"cheaper_inference\"}],\"warnings\":[]}}\n```"
                },
                "examples": {
                  "receipt_opening": {
                    "summary": "Receipt mode: opening frame",
                    "value": "data: {\"type\":\"response.cheaper_inference.request\",\"object\":\"cheaper_inference.request\",\"cheaper_inference\":{\"receipt_version\":1,\"phase\":\"opening\",\"request_id\":\"6f1c2a9e-3b4d-4c5e-8f70-1a2b3c4d5e6f\",\"api_key_id\":\"0b7e9d2c-5a14-4f3b-9c8d-7e6f5a4b3c2d\",\"requested_model\":\"claude-sonnet-4.6\",\"model_lock\":{\"requested\":true,\"enforced\":true}}}\n\n"
                  },
                  "receipt_final": {
                    "summary": "Receipt mode: final frame",
                    "value": "data: {\"type\":\"response.cheaper_inference.receipt\",\"object\":\"cheaper_inference.receipt\",\"cheaper_inference\":{\"receipt_version\":1,\"phase\":\"final\",\"request_id\":\"6f1c2a9e-3b4d-4c5e-8f70-1a2b3c4d5e6f\",\"api_key_id\":\"0b7e9d2c-5a14-4f3b-9c8d-7e6f5a4b3c2d\",\"requested_model\":\"claude-sonnet-4.6\",\"served_model\":\"claude-sonnet-4.6\",\"model_lock\":{\"requested\":true,\"enforced\":true},\"complete\":true,\"billing\":{\"status\":\"settled\",\"billed_cost_usd\":\"0.004213\",\"currency\":\"USD\",\"usage_known\":true,\"basis\":\"ledger\",\"zero_data_retention\":false},\"tokens\":{\"input\":1820,\"output\":214,\"cache_read\":1536,\"cache_write\":0,\"reasoning\":0},\"prompt_cache_mode\":\"on\",\"techniques\":[{\"slug\":\"model-routing\",\"outcome\":\"skipped\",\"reason\":\"model_lock\",\"tokens_saved\":0,\"version\":null,\"layer\":\"cheaper_inference\"}],\"warnings\":[]}}\n\n"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Malformed request (`type: invalid_request_error`, `code: invalid_request`) Under the client contract also `code: invalid_contract_header` (a bad `x-ci-model-lock` or `x-ci-stream-receipt` value) and `code: model_lock_conflict` (Model Lock combined with an experiment). While the key has an open task budget (`/v1/keys/self/task-budgets`), also `code: task_budget_exhausted` (`param: task_budget`): the request's worst-case charge does not fit what the budget has left, so it was refused before anything was held and nothing was charged. Only with a contract header, when the workspace policy requires a task budget and the key has none open, also `code: task_budget_required` (`param: task_budget`); nothing was held or charged. Only with a contract header, every 402, 403 and 429 refusal on the inference path is answered as this 400 instead, with one of these codes: `code: workspace_monthly_cap_hit` (`param: workspace_monthly_cap`), `code: member_monthly_cap_hit` (`param: member_monthly_cap`), `code: wallet_too_low` (`param: wallet`), `code: wallet_top_up_failed` (`param: wallet`), `code: key_monthly_cap_hit` (`param: key_monthly_cap`), `code: contract_funding_refused`, `code: workspace_membership_ended` (`param: workspace_membership`), `code: key_scope_missing` (`param`: the missing scope), `code: key_network_refused` (`param: key_network`), `code: key_allowlist_refused` (`param: key_allowlist`), `code: key_policy_refused` (`param: key_policy`), `code: provider_policy_block` (`param: end_user`), `code: contract_access_refused`, `code: key_minute_cap_hit` (`param: key_minute_cap`), `code: key_daily_cap_hit` (`param: key_daily_cap`), `code: key_parallel_cap_hit` (`param: key_parallel_cap`), `code: contract_pacing_refused`. Each message starts with a distinct phrase and nothing was charged unless it says otherwise. Without a contract header these refusals keep their usual status and code.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Invalid or missing API key (`type: authentication_error`, `code: invalid_api_key`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "402": {
            "description": "Insufficient wallet balance (`type: invalid_request_error`, `code: insufficient_balance`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "The API key lacks the scope this endpoint requires (`type: permission_denied_error`, `code: permission_denied`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found (`type: invalid_request_error`, `code: not_found`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "408": {
            "description": "Request timed out (`type: invalid_request_error`, `code: request_failed`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Conflict (`type: invalid_request_error`, `code: conflict`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "413": {
            "description": "Request too large (`type: invalid_request_error`, `code: request_too_large`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "A parameter failed validation (`type: invalid_request_error`, `code: invalid_request`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "425": {
            "description": "Too early (`type: invalid_request_error`, `code: request_failed`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "Rate limited (`type: rate_limit_error`, `code: rate_limit_exceeded`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Server error (`type: api_error`, `code: server_error`) Under Model Lock also `code: model_lock_violation`: a stage would have served another model, so the request was refused before reaching any model and nothing was billed.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "502": {
            "description": "The upstream provider returned an unusable response (`type: api_error`, `code: upstream_error`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "Service unavailable (`type: api_error`, `code: service_unavailable`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "504": {
            "description": "Upstream timeout (`type: api_error`, `code: upstream_timeout`)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenAIError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/completions": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "Chat"
        ],
        "summary": "Create a text completion",
        "operationId": "createCompletion",
        "description": "OpenAI-compatible legacy completions.",
        "security": [
          {
            "BearerAuth": []
          },
          {
            "AnthropicApiKey": []
          }
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "x-ci-model-lock",
            "in": "header",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Model Lock. Serve exactly the model named in the body: no model-routing technique, no experiment variant and no admission canary may substitute it. Combined with `X-CI-Experiment` (or a forced experiment variant) it is refused with 400 `model_lock_conflict` before anything is read or reserved. If any stage would still change the model, the request is refused with 500 `model_lock_violation` before reaching a model and nothing is billed. Model routing is held off even when the key, the workspace or `x-ci-route` turns it on. `1` or `true` (any case) turns it on; absent or empty leaves it off. Any other value, including `0` and `false`, is refused with 400 `invalid_contract_header` naming the header in `param`, so a typo never silently means off.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "1",
                "true"
              ]
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CompletionRequest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful response",
            "headers": {
              "x-ci-zdr": {
                "description": "Whether zero data retention applied to this request. Absent when no policy was recorded.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "true",
                    "false"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "x-ci-discount-percent": {
                "description": "Quoted customer rate discount versus list, not the final effective savings after usage and optimizations. See usage history for the settled effective discount.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "X-Cheaper-Inference-Request-Id": {
                "description": "Request identifier. Legacy name, still emitted; identical to x-ci-request-id.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "uuid"
                }
              },
              "x-ci-request-id": {
                "description": "Request identifier. Canonical going forward.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
